From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hannes Janetzek <hannes.janetzek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:35:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Engines: run interactive engine shells with TERM=dumb

Engines like fluidsynth are driven through pexpect, waiting for their
prompt. With a terminal type in the environment (a terminal, or the cage
session's TERM=linux) readline switches on bracketed paste and prints
"\x1b[?2004h> ", so fluidsynth's "\n> " prompt never matched: zynthian
waited 30 s and fluidsynth ran without a soundfont, silent. ZynthianOS's
systemd service has no TERM, which readline treats like dumb.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 61dcd7e350df32201fbb0509866576478b32e30f)
---
 zyngine/zynthian_engine.py | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/zyngine/zynthian_engine.py b/zyngine/zynthian_engine.py
index 88b6ec62..927f7f5b 100644
--- a/zyngine/zynthian_engine.py
+++ b/zyngine/zynthian_engine.py
@@ -67,6 +67,11 @@ class zynthian_basic_engine:
         self.proc_exit = False
         self.command = command
         self.command_env = os.environ.copy()
+        # Engines' interactive shells are driven through pexpect. With a terminal type set
+        # (from a terminal or a desktop session; ZynthianOS's systemd service has none),
+        # readline switches on bracketed paste and prefixes its prompt with "\x1b[?2004h",
+        # so the prompt never matches (fluidsynth timed out on postmarketOS).
+        self.command_env['TERM'] = "dumb"
         self.command_prompt = prompt
         self.command_cwd = cwd
         self.ignore_not_on_gui = False
